      "narrative": "The copper lamps flicker as you approach Mara Venn's table. She looks up from a cup of wine that she's been pushing around without drinking, her sharp eyes clocking your movement before you've taken three steps.\n\n\"Ash Gate?\" She sets the cup down. Her voice carries the weight of someone who's been waiting to be asked. \"You're not the first to wonder. It's been shut three days now. Since Old Bram was found.\"\n\nShe leans forward, charcoal coat creaking. Her gaze drifts past you toward the shuttered window \u2014 toward the gate itself.\n\n\"Bram was the ferryman. Had the only key to the Grey Hind, the boat that passes through the Gate. They found him at the landing with his throat torn open. No weapon. No sign of struggle. Just... gone.\"\n\nShe pauses, letting the quiet settle.\n\n\"The Kestrel Guild slammed the Gate shut the same morning. Said it was a 'safety measure.' But here's what doesn't sit right with me.\" She taps the table once. \"Toran Vex \u2014\" she nods toward the ink-stained clerk hunched over a ledger at the bar, \"\u2014 he's the lockwright who kept the Gate's mechanism working for years. Sworn to the Guild. And he hasn't spoken a word about it to anyone. Not one.\"\n\nHer eyes lock onto yours.\n\n\"So either the Guild knows something they're not telling, or Toran's scared of something worse than a dead ferryman. You want my guess? Someone wanted that Gate shut. Permanently. And they killed Bram to make sure no one could open it.\"\n\nShe leans back, letting you process. \"Now. What's your interest in a sealed gate, stranger?\""
    },
