      "narrative": "Mara Venn's cup stops halfway to her lips. She sets it down slowly.\n\n\"That's...\" She frowns, genuinely working through it. \"That's the thing. I've been asking that same question for three days, and every answer I get slips through my fingers like smoke.\"\n\nShe rubs her thumb along the rim of her cup.\n\n\"Bram collected the fares. Everyone knew that. You'd find him at the landing, coin purse at his belt, and he'd wave you onto the Grey Hind. But when I asked who set the prices, who kept the schedule, who decided who was allowed through and who was turned away...\" She shakes her head. \"Bram always said 'the Guild.' Just 'the Guild.' Like that was supposed to be enough.\"\n\nHer jaw tightens.\n\n\"I pressed him once, a few weeks back. Asked for a name. He got real quiet, real fast, and told me to drop it. Said some doors stay shut for a reason.\" She meets your eyes. \"I thought he meant the Gate. Now I'm not so sure.\"\n\nShe leans back, and there's a flicker of frustration in her voice.\n\n\"I don't have a name, Kael. I've scraped this town for one and come up bleeding empty. Whoever sold passage through that Gate \u2014 they made sure Bram was the only face anyone saw.\""
    },
